WEBVTT

01:47.065 --> 01:48.775
Can you see that, everyone?

01:49.526 --> 01:51.069
That's a military plane.

01:51.152 --> 01:52.654
Inside of it

01:52.737 --> 01:55.073
is what's been causing a stir in the US.

01:55.156 --> 01:59.035
I guess you could call it a primitive man.
Right, Professor Kawamoto?

01:59.119 --> 02:00.954
Well, I guess so.

02:01.746 --> 02:04.415
<i>They do say he was revived
from the Jurassic period.</i>

02:05.416 --> 02:07.085
<i>Yes, so they do.</i>

02:08.169 --> 02:11.172
<i>Oh! Is that him?</i>

02:11.256 --> 02:12.674
<i>Yes, that's him!</i>

02:12.757 --> 02:16.678
<i>He's arrived,
guarded by a crowd of soldiers.</i>

02:16.761 --> 02:17.637
That's him.

02:19.514 --> 02:20.557
<i>He's enormous.</i>

02:20.640 --> 02:22.892
<i>At least two meters tall, maybe more.</i>

02:22.976 --> 02:25.186
<i>Wow, he's got quite a glare.</i>

02:25.270 --> 02:26.938
<i>Seems he's on his guard.</i>

02:27.522 --> 02:29.440
<i>He's checking his surroundings.</i>

02:34.028 --> 02:35.071
Captain.

02:36.489 --> 02:38.950
This dude... he's strong.

02:39.659 --> 02:42.287
He's really quite savage.

02:42.370 --> 02:44.581
He gives off a very primitive air.

02:45.456 --> 02:46.833
Are you with us, Ms. Aizawa?

02:47.417 --> 02:50.086
<i>Will you see if you can get him to chat?</i>

02:50.170 --> 02:52.463
Sure. I'll see what I can do!

02:54.174 --> 02:55.842
- Excuse me!
- No!

02:55.925 --> 02:57.468
- No!
- Hello...

03:06.686 --> 03:08.354
No!

03:11.941 --> 03:12.859
What?!

03:13.526 --> 03:14.861
Oh, uh...

03:16.446 --> 03:17.614
No!

03:21.868 --> 03:24.454
<i>Pitifully savage.</i>

03:31.794 --> 03:34.005
<i>Absurdly savage.</i>

03:36.758 --> 03:38.301
<i>All of Japan witnessed it.</i>

03:38.801 --> 03:42.597
<i>His savagery is so innate,
metaphors cannot do it justice.</i>

03:43.348 --> 03:44.182
Stop rolling!

03:44.265 --> 03:46.851
<i>Some struggled to gain control
of the situation.</i>

03:46.935 --> 03:48.770
<i>Some were unable to accept it.</i>

03:49.812 --> 03:51.439
<i>Everyone reacted differently,</i>

03:52.106 --> 03:54.776
<i>but their attention was fixed
on only one thing.</i>

03:56.236 --> 03:59.697
<i>Just what will this male do next?</i>

04:00.907 --> 04:02.784
<i>What action will he take?</i>

04:04.994 --> 04:07.830
<i>With all of Japan waiting
with bated breath...</i>

04:09.457 --> 04:10.291
<i>the male...</i>

04:21.928 --> 04:23.054
<i>went to sleep.</i>

04:26.891 --> 04:29.686
This is merely my theory.

04:30.395 --> 04:32.522
<i>The 100 million years of the dinosaurs,</i>

04:32.605 --> 04:35.817
<i>from the Jurassic
to the Cretaceous periods,</i>

04:35.900 --> 04:37.443
<i>came to a sudden end</i>

04:37.527 --> 04:40.613
<i>when a giant meteor struck the Earth.</i>

04:41.281 --> 04:43.866
<i>I think everyone knows the story this far.</i>

04:44.534 --> 04:46.953
<i>But when the giant meteor collided,</i>

04:47.787 --> 04:50.832
<i>what exactly happened then?</i>

04:51.791 --> 04:54.585
<i>An enormous cloud of dust
billowed into the atmosphere,</i>

04:54.669 --> 04:56.587
<i>blocking out the sun's heat.</i>

04:56.671 --> 05:01.259
<i>The surface of the Earth was instantly
plunged to the same temperature as space,</i>

05:01.342 --> 05:04.846
<i>negative 270.4 degrees Celsius.</i>

05:05.930 --> 05:09.142
<i>Everything on Earth became frozen.</i>

05:09.225 --> 05:11.352
<i>The giant dinosaurs and the insects,</i>

05:11.978 --> 05:14.105
<i>as well as all battles.</i>

05:15.106 --> 05:18.609
<i>The impact shifted the plates
of the Earth's crust.</i>

05:18.693 --> 05:22.322
<i>As a result,
the usually stable salt rock stratum</i>

05:22.405 --> 05:25.616
<i>preserved this battle.</i>

05:26.200 --> 05:29.829
<i>As for the two beings
discovered preserved in salt earlier,</i>

05:29.912 --> 05:33.624
<i>one was too badly damaged to revive.</i>

05:35.585 --> 05:38.254
<i>But one remained whole.</i>

05:38.338 --> 05:41.966
As for the incident earlier
at Haneda Airport,

05:42.550 --> 05:46.929
I feel nothing but regret for
the female reporter who was the victim.

05:47.722 --> 05:51.934
However, you must understand he came
from the Earth 200 million years ago,

05:52.018 --> 05:55.021
which may as well be
a completely different planet.

05:55.104 --> 05:58.024
The values and morals that we all hold

05:58.107 --> 06:00.526
mean absolutely nothing to him.

06:05.490 --> 06:07.158
HAND PICKLE OVER!!

06:08.409 --> 06:10.495
Can you see what's happening here?

06:10.578 --> 06:14.165
Ordinary citizens have descended
on the front gate of the US military base.

06:15.333 --> 06:17.877
Since the victim
was a popular news reporter,

06:17.960 --> 06:20.338
there are hundreds of demonstrators.

06:20.922 --> 06:26.928
The US military has not made any comment
regarding the rape by the primitive man.

06:27.011 --> 06:30.431
Due to this, the demonstrators' anger
has reached its peak.

06:33.059 --> 06:34.936
I know Pickle's here.

06:35.895 --> 06:37.021
I'm comin' through.

06:55.915 --> 06:58.960
They built this thing in about a month,

07:00.336 --> 07:02.213
but I'm not so sure about it.

07:02.296 --> 07:04.090
A tire. Magazines.

07:04.173 --> 07:05.216
A fish tank.

07:05.842 --> 07:07.218
And this.

07:08.010 --> 07:11.097
It seems too obvious and simple.

07:12.515 --> 07:14.142
I wonder if he even enjoys it.

07:14.809 --> 07:17.520
Shut up. We're being watched.

07:23.609 --> 07:26.487
<i>It's almost like sneaking into
a woman's bedroom.</i>

07:27.822 --> 07:30.992
<i>What was I thinking, sneaking in here?</i>

07:32.493 --> 07:34.996
<i>Since that TV broadcast...</i>

07:35.663 --> 07:39.750
<i>This urge started the moment
I laid eyes on that mysterious savage.</i>

07:40.835 --> 07:41.794
<i>A guard.</i>

07:42.503 --> 07:43.754
<i>He's coming this way.</i>

08:05.485 --> 08:08.404
<i>I can get around like this
for the time being.</i>

08:11.491 --> 08:12.742
Fools.

08:16.412 --> 08:18.247
Stand back, protestors.

08:18.748 --> 08:20.416
These guys are gonna go flyin'!

08:25.505 --> 08:27.089
TAMOTSU ISHIZUKA (34), DEMONSTRATOR

08:27.173 --> 08:31.552
It was really hot near him,
like an engine or something.

08:33.471 --> 08:34.555
<i>Then suddenly,</i>

08:34.639 --> 08:37.058
<i>the soldiers started punching each other</i>

08:37.141 --> 08:39.560
<i>right in front of the guy in black.</i>

08:40.353 --> 08:42.647
<i>The last guy didn't even try to stop them.</i>

08:42.730 --> 08:44.649
<i>He started punching himself!</i>

08:46.025 --> 08:48.945
<i>The man in black just stood and watched.</i>

08:50.154 --> 08:53.658
<i>Eventually, he walked up to the gate.</i>

08:54.158 --> 08:56.327
<i>The soldiers continued
to punch each other.</i>

08:57.078 --> 08:58.829
<i>It was like, you know,</i>

08:58.913 --> 09:02.833
<i>when unruly brothers are caught
doing mischief by their strict father</i>

09:03.417 --> 09:05.920
<i>and they try to pin the blame
on each other.</i>

09:06.420 --> 09:10.841
<i>Like they were punishing themselves
before their father could punish them.</i>

09:11.801 --> 09:15.846
<i>Even though they were bleeding,
losing their teeth, and swelling up,</i>

09:16.472 --> 09:19.225
<i>the three men didn't try to stop.</i>

09:20.184 --> 09:21.018
<i>But then...</i>

09:21.686 --> 09:22.520
Stop!

09:23.563 --> 09:26.065
<i>It was like an order
from the commander-in-chief.</i>

09:26.148 --> 09:28.025
<i>They stopped instantly.</i>

09:29.026 --> 09:30.611
<i>Then he said something strange.</i>

09:31.404 --> 09:33.364
You men made the right choice.

09:33.864 --> 09:38.077
If even one of you had run off
instead of fighting,

09:38.160 --> 09:40.288
I would've slaughtered you then and there.

09:41.789 --> 09:44.834
But if you'd attacked me,
your fate would've been the same.

09:45.835 --> 09:49.547
So, as a last resort,
you decided to harm one another,

09:50.214 --> 09:52.300
to harm yourself.

09:52.967 --> 09:55.636
That was best. The right thing to do.

09:57.597 --> 09:58.806
I'll forgive you.

09:59.640 --> 10:01.684
<i>What was their expression then?</i>

10:02.268 --> 10:03.728
<i>They looked relieved.</i>

10:04.270 --> 10:06.105
<i>It was clear to anyone watching</i>

10:06.188 --> 10:08.399
<i>that they felt relieved
to their very cores.</i>

10:08.941 --> 10:11.819
<i>But they were plainly beaten to a pulp.</i>

10:13.863 --> 10:17.575
<i>Well, I mean, he just cut right through
the lock. With his bare hand.</i>

10:22.038 --> 10:25.082
<i>Then he went inside,
like it was his own home.</i>

10:25.166 --> 10:28.377
<i>No, nobody stopped him.
It was way too dangerous to.</i>

10:30.296 --> 10:35.426
<i>As long as I match my breathing to his,
this soldier won't notice me.</i>

10:36.344 --> 10:37.386
<i>The real problem,</i>

10:38.554 --> 10:43.100
<i>is where on this large military base
the primitive man is hidden.</i>

10:44.060 --> 10:46.187
<i>Where is he on this huge base?</i>

10:51.442 --> 10:52.276
Hi.

10:52.360 --> 10:53.194
Hi.

10:54.236 --> 10:56.364
This is such a pain in the ass.

10:57.448 --> 10:58.407
You mean Pickle?

10:59.283 --> 11:00.910
I'm on patrol 'til morning.

11:00.993 --> 11:02.745
Aw man. That sucks.

11:02.828 --> 11:04.872
When I'm done, let's grab a drink.

11:04.955 --> 11:07.249
- Sure. See ya.
- Later.

11:14.465 --> 11:15.549
<i>I'm in luck.</i>

11:16.175 --> 11:19.387
<i>If I stick with this soldier,
he'll take me to the primitive man.</i>

11:24.684 --> 11:25.518
<i>This must be it.</i>

11:26.852 --> 11:27.687
Huh?

11:33.192 --> 11:34.026
<i>Sorry.</i>

11:43.411 --> 11:45.955
<i>This must be
where the primitive man is kept.</i>

11:46.831 --> 11:48.249
<i>A base within the base.</i>

12:06.225 --> 12:07.059
<i>It's open.</i>

12:10.855 --> 12:12.815
<i>And this one's open too.</i>

12:14.608 --> 12:17.027
<i>It's as if someone snuck in before me.</i>

12:22.324 --> 12:23.325
Huh?

12:24.118 --> 12:25.077
You're...

12:29.874 --> 12:31.959
Kosho Shinogi.

12:32.460 --> 12:33.836
Sea King Retsu.

12:34.545 --> 12:35.713
<i>Why...</i>

12:36.255 --> 12:37.089
<i>Are you here?</i>

12:42.261 --> 12:43.512
So, you too, huh?

12:44.555 --> 12:46.265
You're here to see Pickle.

12:49.435 --> 12:52.104
His strength is apparent at a glance.

12:52.188 --> 12:56.358
His savagery is so deep, he mates
without a care for who's watching.

12:56.942 --> 13:01.614
With the flame of curiosity lit,
you suddenly find yourself on this base.

13:03.199 --> 13:05.826
I want to meet him. I want to see him.

13:06.869 --> 13:10.122
And, if possible, I want to fight him.

13:11.081 --> 13:13.793
It appears that we are both
thinking the same thing.

13:14.960 --> 13:16.921
We are kindred spirits,

13:17.004 --> 13:19.715
and should welcome one another
with a warm handshake.

13:19.799 --> 13:21.133
But that won't happen.

13:22.927 --> 13:24.470
I got here first.

13:26.972 --> 13:28.140
Any complaints?

13:38.025 --> 13:39.902
Hey, Shinogi.

13:40.611 --> 13:42.655
You're not the first one here.

13:43.280 --> 13:44.406
Doppo!

13:51.497 --> 13:52.414
Jack!

13:56.502 --> 13:58.170
Goki!

14:01.090 --> 14:03.843
I was trying to find the right timing,

14:03.926 --> 14:05.928
but it seems I can't wait.

14:06.512 --> 14:08.222
Katsumi Orochi?

14:08.305 --> 14:09.682
I see.

14:10.766 --> 14:13.686
So that's what's up here.

14:14.436 --> 14:15.938
Sea King Jaku.

14:16.021 --> 14:18.190
Retsu, long time no see.

14:19.108 --> 14:22.027
This is one hell of a reunion.

14:22.820 --> 14:24.947
This is getting embarrassing.

14:25.030 --> 14:28.868
The old and the young,
covering ourselves in black,

14:28.951 --> 14:30.452
as if we're playing ninjas.

14:30.536 --> 14:34.206
Yep, this is pretty embarrassing.

14:35.708 --> 14:37.668
Jaku, even you came?

14:37.751 --> 14:41.964
Huh? Surely you kid me, Man Eater Orochi.

14:42.047 --> 14:45.759
Social education is an important aspect
of martial arts.

14:45.843 --> 14:50.681
Teaching it is a vital task that helps
promising youth live life properly.

14:50.764 --> 14:52.558
"Promising youth"?

14:53.058 --> 14:55.477
Are you talking about Pickle?

14:56.103 --> 14:58.063
Well, yes.

14:58.564 --> 15:00.399
We're all a similar breed.

15:00.482 --> 15:02.401
We wanna fight so badly we can't stand it.

15:02.484 --> 15:04.111
That's why we broke in.

15:04.194 --> 15:07.615
Now that is a true martial artist.

15:07.698 --> 15:10.868
To be honest, that's exactly what we are.

15:12.161 --> 15:13.120
In that case...

15:14.914 --> 15:16.373
<i>Who will fight Pickle?</i>

15:16.457 --> 15:21.003
But before that,
we'd better see what Pickle's up to.

15:26.258 --> 15:27.134
He's sleepin'.

15:27.718 --> 15:32.514
Look at him takin' it easy,
even with all this commotion out here.

15:32.598 --> 15:36.518
Do you really think he's taking it easy?

15:37.603 --> 15:40.898
I wonder if he even thinks
we're his enemies.

15:47.988 --> 15:49.406
He woke... Whoa!

16:11.011 --> 16:14.264
Welcome, Pickle, to the future.

16:16.016 --> 16:18.185
Looks like we're all here.

16:20.646 --> 16:23.440
What a ragtag mob.

16:26.652 --> 16:30.072
Hey, who are you callin' a ragtag mob?

16:33.033 --> 16:35.703
That's why nobody wants to be around you.

16:35.786 --> 16:38.455
Not me, not Baki, not even your father.

16:41.417 --> 16:45.963
You come in here without any plan
and just figure it'll work out.

16:46.588 --> 16:48.799
Even though you sense that you'll lose,

16:48.882 --> 16:52.219
you can't help but put on
a brave show for your father.

16:52.845 --> 16:55.014
And if you avoid getting killed instantly,

16:55.097 --> 16:57.725
you know you can count on getting help.

16:58.642 --> 17:00.561
<i>He knew exactly what he was thinking.</i>

17:00.644 --> 17:03.814
<i>He saw right through
the young karate fighter.</i>

17:04.732 --> 17:07.651
<i>There was only one thing for him to do.</i>

17:19.580 --> 17:22.082
Go play cat's cradle in the corner.

17:30.174 --> 17:31.008
Outta the way!

17:32.426 --> 17:33.510
I'm comin' in.

17:33.594 --> 17:34.511
But...

17:35.137 --> 17:35.971
Fool.

18:00.621 --> 18:01.622
I'm here.

18:02.372 --> 18:03.791
Pickle.

18:04.541 --> 18:09.630
You're a warrior from ancient Earth,
but you're named after a salted vegetable.

18:10.964 --> 18:13.050
If you can't understand what I say,

18:13.133 --> 18:14.802
then sense my meaning,

18:16.220 --> 18:18.430
<i>like an infant
who can't understand language</i>

18:18.514 --> 18:21.391
<i>understands their mother's love.</i>

18:21.892 --> 18:25.312
Know in your heart
our feelings toward you.

18:26.313 --> 18:29.817
The eight assembled here, as well as I,

18:30.609 --> 18:32.152
have come to fight you.

18:33.695 --> 18:34.780
<i>During that era</i>

18:34.863 --> 18:37.449
<i>when the most powerful creatures
roamed the Earth,</i>

18:37.533 --> 18:39.993
<i>you fed on the most powerful in history.</i>

18:41.829 --> 18:43.497
<i>If you merely wanted to eat,</i>

18:43.580 --> 18:46.416
<i>there were other ways
you could have done that.</i>

18:47.501 --> 18:49.461
But instead, you went after it.

18:50.045 --> 18:51.463
You've piqued my interest.

19:27.332 --> 19:28.250
Bastard.

19:28.876 --> 19:31.253
He made me pull a move.

19:36.258 --> 19:37.509
<i>He stood up.</i>

19:38.343 --> 19:40.012
<i>That simple action alone</i>

19:40.762 --> 19:43.265
<i>captivated the eyes of all the warriors.</i>

19:44.433 --> 19:47.227
<i>By submitting to civilization,</i>

19:47.311 --> 19:50.063
<i>many of our body's abilities
have disappeared.</i>

19:50.772 --> 19:53.567
<i>But from a body
that fully maintains those abilities,</i>

19:53.650 --> 19:56.778
<i>even the simplest of actions is beautiful.</i>

19:58.071 --> 20:01.658
<i>Having seen this,
how could they just meekly leave?</i>

20:01.742 --> 20:05.537
<i>The jealousy of the warriors
reached its peak, when...</i>

20:05.621 --> 20:07.122
<i>Stop!</i>

20:08.165 --> 20:11.126
Mr. Yujiro Hanma. Hold it right there.

20:12.628 --> 20:14.087
<i>Come out.</i>

20:14.171 --> 20:16.798
<i>The building is completely surrounded.</i>

20:25.849 --> 20:28.685
I'm sorry to bother you
while you were enjoying yourself.

20:28.769 --> 20:33.899
I am Commander Henry
of company two of the 301st Battalion.

20:34.650 --> 20:38.654
This is a heck of a polite way
to arrest an intruder.

20:38.737 --> 20:40.197
This is not an arrest!

20:40.280 --> 20:43.575
The US Army doesn't have
the ability to arrest you.

20:43.659 --> 20:46.828
How did you know that I was the intruder?

20:47.412 --> 20:51.833
That wasn't an intrusion.
You plainly went through the front gate.

20:52.584 --> 20:57.589
Judging from the fact that the guards
at the gate couldn't call for backup,

20:58.465 --> 21:02.844
I knew it must be the Ogre, Yujiro Hanma.

21:03.679 --> 21:05.847
You've got nerve
trying to curry favor with me.

21:05.931 --> 21:07.599
As a soldier,

21:07.683 --> 21:10.519
I am savoring the honor of meeting you.

21:11.019 --> 21:12.771
So, what do you want?

21:13.981 --> 21:14.940
I'm coming to that.

21:15.691 --> 21:20.404
Pickle is a cultural treasure
to all of humanity.

21:20.487 --> 21:22.364
He is a living world heritage.

21:23.699 --> 21:26.118
Please, withdraw now.

21:28.704 --> 21:29.621
On one condition.

21:31.164 --> 21:32.916
Let the other eight leave as well.

21:34.251 --> 21:36.378
You mean them too?

21:37.087 --> 21:41.883
You know very well that those guys
aren't here to destroy or steal anything.

21:42.718 --> 21:45.387
Like me, they just came to say hello.

21:46.179 --> 21:48.515
But if you don't like it, that's fine.

21:49.391 --> 21:50.642
No!

21:54.062 --> 21:56.648
<i>And thus, the curtain peacefully closed</i>

21:56.732 --> 21:59.651
<i>on the saga of the world's
most fearsome evening intrusion.</i>

22:00.235 --> 22:02.154
I like that look in your eye, son.

22:03.196 --> 22:07.909
<i>The warriors were released
ten kilometers from the military base.</i>

22:09.161 --> 22:10.829
<i>All except for one.</i>

22:11.455 --> 22:14.041
Eight, huh? He totally knew I was here.

22:16.418 --> 22:17.377
Nice meetin' ya.
